      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="683832709">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP486 - Odstone Green Park - and finally the park is green! Another quick find. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Road trip! Iron Phoenix and I had a fantastic caching and capping from Calgary to Red Deer. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683668004">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP486 - Odstone Green Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, this time in Red Deer!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A nice little park tucked away for playing ball with friends or chasing the dogs around! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; We did neither today, as we were on a quest for caps! It was a nice quick find that I could almost reach my arm out to get the info! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_wink.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Beautiful cap in great shape!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683269157">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-02T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP486  Odstone Green Park - Pretty much a park and grab with this one.  My last Red Deer cap.  Found some on the trip north on Sunday and quite a few more today.  A nice way to tour some of the areas of a town I have never spent much time in. Thanks ofth.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682464161">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2389197">KinderKen</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP486 - Odstone Green Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I headed back up to Red Deer today to find a few more brass caps and this was the third of five. It was a quick find and thanks for the cap. The information is on it's way.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="680245881">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1636194">behmSquad</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP486 Odstone Green Park&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#13 of 46 caps found on the day.  I spent the early morning finding caps at all points from Calgary to Red Deer.  I returned to Calgary in the afternoon to clear out much of north Calgary including a good hike across nose hill.  TFTC&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
